\] The function $y = x+2$ is a linear function and takes on all real values except at the point where $x = -1$. When $x = -1$, $y = -1 + 2 = 1$. Since the function is undefined at $x = -1$, the value $y = 1$ is not in the range. Therefore, the range of the function is all real numbers except $1$. The range is $(-\infty, 1) \cup (1, \infty)$. </think> <answer> $(-\infty, 1) \cup (1, \infty)$ </answer>

